WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.734
Good morning, it's Thursday, November 19.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:09.802
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:17.870
Today: Anthropic prices its IPO above range, Gemini 3.6 Flash retires today, and OVHcloud opens its sovereign AI summit.

00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:19.803
First, the story of the day.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:31.539
Anthropic priced its initial public offering at eighty-three dollars per share on Wednesday, November eighteenth, above the expected range of seventy to seventy-eight dollars.

00:00:31.605 --> 00:00:39.740
According to the Washington Examiner, it is selling 980 million Class A shares in what would be the largest IPO on record.

00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:43.541
Reports put the valuation at about 1.5 trillion dollars.

00:00:43.607 --> 00:00:50.942
Shares are expected to start trading on Nasdaq under the ticker A N T on Thursday, November nineteenth, today.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:58.410
Yahoo, relaying the Associated Press, says the pricing signals investor appetite for AI despite bubble worries.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.341
The read here: nothing in your contract changes at the opening bell.

00:01:03.405 --> 00:01:05.825
What changes is the disclosure regime.

00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:13.340
A frontier vendor now reports every quarter, and each report will show commitments, margins and capacity constraints.

00:01:13.404 --> 00:01:16.015
That is useful input for a risk register.

00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:26.079
Pricing above the range likely gives the vendor room to keep investing in capacity, but that is a prediction, not a promise about your prices or your quotas.

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:30.855
A much larger share count also means more public scrutiny of its spending.

00:01:30.919 --> 00:01:34.422
For a platform team, the practical steps stay the same.

00:01:34.486 --> 00:01:37.670
Keep a second vendor routable through the gateway.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:38.753
Time a failover.

00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:41.683
Review the vendor's disclosures each quarter.

00:01:41.746 --> 00:01:45.950
And ignore first-day price swings when you make routing decisions.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.341
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:01:48.402 --> 00:01:52.416
OVHcloud holds its AI Summit in Paris today, November nineteenth.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:02:02.172
The company's own event page frames it around sovereign AI, from infrastructure to models, with its leaders presenting AI strategy and product announcements.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:05.938
A beta of OVHai Workspace is expected to be announced there.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.360
Nothing from the event itself was available before this briefing, so no announcement is described here.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.362
Why it matters: today is a pitch, not capacity.

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:25.700
When the announcements land, sort each one into three boxes: what you can order now, what is a beta, and what is only a roadmap.

00:02:25.772 --> 00:02:35.472
Then compare with the hyperscaler sovereign offers on four points: where models run, who operates them, who holds the keys, and price.

00:02:35.545 --> 00:02:44.810
A European option earns a place in your gateway only when it passes your own evaluation set and has a published price and quota.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.340
Next, Platform.

00:02:46.402 --> 00:02:57.187
Google's documentation lists November nineteenth as the retirement date of Gemini 3.6 Flash on its Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform, with Gemini 3.8 Flash as the replacement.

00:02:57.249 --> 00:03:04.998
The model was released there on July twenty-first and is available in the global endpoint and in the US and EU multi-regions.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:16.589
Google notes that retirement dates apply to support on that platform, that models may remain reachable through the Gemini API, and that timelines may be extended but never moved earlier.

00:03:16.651 --> 00:03:21.300
Its policy gives at least forty-five days to migrate once a date is posted.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.453
What this really signals: model lifetimes are now measured in months.

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:28.762
This one lasted about four months.

00:03:28.828 --> 00:03:35.030
For a platform team, treat retirement dates as data in the gateway, not as emails in an inbox.

00:03:35.096 --> 00:03:36.877
Alert well before the date.

00:03:36.943 --> 00:03:41.694
Rerun your evaluation set on the successor before the switch, not after.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.566
And check that your fallback route does not point at another model on the same calendar.

00:03:47.632 --> 00:03:52.910
A forced migration is a quality event and a cost event, so budget time for both.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.960
The number of the day.

00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:56.937
Eighty-three dollars a share.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:04:03.066
That is Anthropic's IPO price, above the expected range of seventy to seventy-eight dollars.

00:04:03.132 --> 00:04:07.745
Investor appetite for AI is running stronger than the range suggested.

00:04:07.811 --> 00:04:08.734
What to watch.

00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:16.708
Today, November nineteenth: Anthropic's first trade, OVHcloud's AI Summit in Paris, and the Gemini 3.6 Flash retirement.

00:04:16.774 --> 00:04:19.871
Microsoft Ignite runs until November twentieth.

00:04:19.937 --> 00:04:23.957
Walmart's Agent Profiles are due about November twenty-first.

00:04:24.023 --> 00:04:36.083
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 requests reroute December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:04:36.149 --> 00:04:38.060
And a question for your team.

00:04:38.126 --> 00:04:48.671
Which of your production routes point at a model with a retirement date in the next ninety days, and does your gateway warn you before the notice window closes?

00:04:48.737 --> 00:04:50.055
That's it for today.

00:04:50.121 --> 00:04:52.691
Sources are in the episode description.

00:04:52.757 --> 00:04:54.734
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:55.920
See you tomorrow.
